  <notes>Justification (CLAUDE.md §11): Existing -- H14's parent orchestration + 2 sub-handlers are already correct; only 1 collaborator is a shell-out. Extension -- reusing task 125's SecretClient pattern for this reader is the minimal correct move. Cost-of-doing-nothing -- H14 cannot execute under Option D's zero-shell main site even though 3 of its 4 collaborators are otherwise ready.

COMPLETION (2026-08-20): New SecretClientKvReader.cs (Azure.Security.KeyVault.Secrets SecretClient.GetSecretAsync, same Success/NotFound/Failure contract as the retired reader; explicit 403-vs-404-vs-generic classification per task 143/144 verification discipline). AzCliKvSecretReader.cs retired -- kept on disk unregistered with a retirement banner (task 125's AzCliKvSecretsWriter precedent: this project's uniform convention regardless of whether the retired type has dedicated tests, which it never did). IntegrationWiringOptions gained KvReadTimeout + a scoped NFR-05 Validate() (KvReadTimeout only -- the 7 pre-existing H14a/b/c fields were deliberately left out of the boot-time gate, out of this task's declared scope). IntegrationWiringModule swapped Configure&lt;T&gt;() for AddOptions&lt;T&gt;().Bind().Validate().ValidateOnStart() and the IKvSecretReader registration from a plain type mapping to a factory lambda resolving the shared UAMI-pinned TokenCredential (parity with SecretClientKvWriter's Worker/Program.cs registration). 7 new tests (SecretClientKvReaderTests.cs, fake-transport ADR-038 path #1) covering happy path, NotFound, 403 access-denied distinction, empty-value-on-200, generic 500, timeout, and a source-text grep test proving zero 'az'/ProcessStartInfo references remain. H14/H14b/H14c's existing tests (46 total) pass UNMODIFIED. L2 tests: 1067 -&gt; 1074/1074 (+7, zero regressions). Quality gates (code-review + adr-check, FULL rigor + test-modifying override, both unconditional): 0 Critical, 0 Warnings, 0 ADR violations. Commit: see git log.</notes>

